Set verify_jwt=false for paystack-webhook (server-to-server, no Supabase session)

Deploying it with the default JWT-required setting meant Supabase's own
gateway rejected every call with 401 before the function's own
x-paystack-signature check ever ran - confirmed live: Paystack's
webhook caller never carries a Supabase session, so this must stay
off for this one function specifically (every other function keeps
requiring a JWT, since the app calls those with the user's session or
the anon key).

